Z||000000||JayUSA77||08-11-2001||03:23 PM||||Hey guys i thought replacing my outer fiero seals for the window would be a breeze but then i forgot i have a fiero so thats not possible. okay the problem is there is two screws i cant get to do to the fact that the window wont go down far enough for me to get them. What am i missing i have to be doing something wrong. the seal im talking about is the one that wipes the window clean and keeps water from going down into the door. I need major help and ANY advice would be appreciated.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-11-2001||03:44 PM||||I think you would need the tool thats used to remove the dew wipes..<P>you could try to bend a small screwdriver enough to get into there..<P>on rodneys site, he shows a photo of it..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieronv||08-11-2001||03:53 PM||||Look in the cave under dew notes. What you need is a special screwdriver from Rodney Dickman or you can make one yourself. Check out the Michigan clubs site for a good step by step instructions with pictures on how to do this.<P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||08-11-2001||04:08 PM||||Sounds like the "Dew Wipe Blues"!  <P>You CAN remove the screws.  You may have to drill them out from the wrong side or get Rodney Dicknman's very, extra short Phillips.  You might can just grap hold with needle nose pliers.  In any event, just worry them out!  <P>These screws are aaddressed in every mention of replacing dew wipes.  They are a bi+ch to get out and in.  Well worth it , though.  You will be very happy with the results.||||reg||1
