Z||000005||Fiero_Freak||08-11-2001||10:08 PM||||I bought a cheap tip from the hardware store and used a wrench that would hold around the adapter end.  Then I ground the excess off and superglued it in the wrench.  Used it and then used solvent to get it off the wrench.<BR>Or just buy the tool.. It's cheap enough if you can wait for it.  You know you're going to have a 2nd and 3rd Fiero soon.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
